# CQ 12: Which hyperparameters does an algorithm have, and what were they set to?
#
# 3.3.4 defines the hyperparameter as a characteristic of a machine learning
# algorithm affecting its learning process, selected prior to training.
#
# The pattern places it on the algorithm superclass, so a model algorithm and
# an evaluation algorithm may carry one as well. Test case 2 uses that: a rule
# threshold is chosen in advance and steers the behaviour of the procedure, so
# it is a hyperparameter rather than a model parameter.
#
# The value comes through hasSetting rather than through forCharacteristic. A
# hyperparameter is chosen before a training and a quality of clause 3.5 is
# established by one, and the answer stays readable as a list of settings for
# that reason. Optional, since an algorithm may be recorded before its values
# are fixed.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?algorithm ?algorithmKind ?hyperparameter ?setting
WHERE {
  ?algorithm iso:hasHyperparameter ?hyperparameter .
  ?algorithm a ?algorithmKind . ?algorithmKind rdfs:subClassOf* iso:Algorithm .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?algorithm a ?n . ?n rdfs:subClassOf+ ?algorithmKind .
                      ?n rdfs:subClassOf* iso:Algorithm }
  OPTIONAL { ?hyperparameter iso:hasSetting/iso:quantity ?setting }
} ORDER BY ?algorithm ?hyperparameter
